Summary of changes from V6.03.00

Build system
Firmware is now built with pico-sdk 2.3.0 (TinyUSB remains the hand-upgraded 0.20 copy, re-applied over the SDK's bundled version)

All RP2350 versions with camera support
Support for the OV5640 camera: CAMERA OPEN OV5640 with QVGA (320x240) RGB565 capture, motion detection (CAMERA CHANGE) and JPEG capture (CAMERA CAPTURE JPEG) at VGA, XGA, SXGA, UXGA, QXGA and 5MP resolutions with HIGH/MEDIUM/LOW quality
OV5640 white balance is automatically frozen at the live preview's converged setting when taking a JPEG so stills match the preview colour
OV5640 display capture automatically adapts its pixel clock to the CPU speed (378/315/252MHz supported)

All versions with camera support
CAMERA OPEN no longer requires a display: CAMERA CAPTURE JPEG and CAMERA CHANGE (motion detection) work headless; only the simple CAMERA CAPTURE needs a display (any panel with at least RGB565 colour is now accepted, including SSD1963 types)
A misconfigured or disconnected camera now reports a specific error (identifying the stalled signal) instead of freezing the machine
Camera capture no longer disturbs the PSRAM/flash controller: fixes rare hard faults after captures on PSRAM-enabled builds
Faster capture inner loops

Bluetooth versions
Bluetooth console and keyboard fixes

Other
Auto-configure PICO COMPUTER 3 at boot (RP2350)
Fixes embedded pin-status program for WEB builds (pin 84)
Fixes OLIMEXUSB platform string matching
Keyboard map updates
